      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "What fixed it for me:\n\nI've been having the exact same issue for the last week.  The Quest has been bugging me from time to time saying \"You don't have a boundary.  Want to use Stationary?\".  I always click Yes since I don't physically move in VRChat.  This morning, I decided to create a roomscale boundary and the microphone is back to normal.\n\nIt's not a question of OS update during the night or that the headset had reset without me knowing it.  I went in VRChat, tested the microphone and it was bad.  Left, created the roomscale boundary, immediately went back in VRChat and the microphone was fine.",
